meta {
  name: Create App
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/apps
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-Dev-User-ID: {{devUserId}}
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "github_installation_id": 12345678,
    "repo_owner": "ClappFormOrg",
    "repo_name": "govchat",
    "branch": "main"
  }
}

docs {
  Register a new App from a linked GitHub repository. Requires the
  Developer role on the calling user.

  Flow:
    1. resolve `branch` to a commit SHA via the GitHub App
    2. fetch appstore.yaml + run schema validation
    3. fetch every declared evidence file + content-type-check
    4. fetch Chart.yaml + values.schema.json
    5. persist App + AppVersion + AuditSubmission in one transaction
    6. write `app.created` to audit_logs

  Returns:
    201 — created. `app_version.state` will be `draft` until you POST
          /apps/:slug/submit.
    422 — manifest or evidence validation failed (see `errors[]`).
    503 — github_not_configured. Configure GITHUB_APP_* in .env or
          stub via NullClient.
    409 — slug or repo already linked.
}
